      "license": "CC0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
      "artist": "Dhx1",
      "description": "Sign at the SIEV X Memorial at Kurrajong Point, Yarralumla Peninsula, Weston Park, Canberra. The sign reads \"The SIEV X Memorial remembers the 146 children, 142 mothers and 65 fathers who died on the refugee boat SIEV X, at the height of the Federal election campaign in October 2001. The memorial is a shared effort by over 300 schools, churches and community groups across Australia. Each pole remembers one person who died, the samller poles for children and the larger for adults. Our message in making the memorial is that Australia is not a country defined by fear or greed. Love is stronger than fear. Kindness is stronger than greed.\"",
      "dateCreated": "2015-01-03 06:07:42",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "siev-x-wp",
